Measurement structure (inferred from data): {structure_note}.
Sensor assumed stationary at the origin; dt = {dt} (uniform spacing, no gaps in t).
Record: {T} steps, t = {t[0]:.0f}..{t[-1]:.0f}.

FILTER
------
Bootstrap particle filter, N = {N_PART} particles ({n_part_reason}).
State: [px, py, vx, vy, bias_range, bias_bearing] plus a 2-mode Markov-switched
constant-velocity maneuver mode (IMM-style adaptation; transitions
{P_TRANS[0]} / {P_TRANS[1]}, accel sigma {SIG_A}).
Likelihood: Student-t (dof {T_DOF}) per channel with calibrated scales
sigma_range = {s_r:.4f}, sigma_bearing = {s_b:.5f} rad. Scales are anchored at
the robust second-difference noise floor (x3 range, x6 bearing tempering for
model mismatch), then ONE bounded check rescaled them to bring mean NIS into
the 0.7-3.0 band; history (s_r, s_b, resulting mean NIS): {calib_hist}.
Missing channels (mask=False)
are skipped in the likelihood. NO observation was deleted or replaced; outliers
are only soft-down-weighted by the heavy-tailed likelihood.
Angle wrapping: bearing innovations wrapped into (-pi, pi]; {wrap_events}
gap-aware raw wrap event(s) detected (adjacent valid steps only; the first
difference after a NaN gap is excluded by construction), notably the +pi
crossing near t=6.
Systematic resampling when ESS < N/2 -> {resampling_count} events at
t = {summary['resampling_steps']}.
ESS: mean {np.mean(ess):.1f}, min {np.min(ess):.1f} at t={t[int(np.argmin(ess))]:.0f}.
ESS collapsed below 5% of N (transient weight degeneracy, driven by joint
outlier bursts and the fast bearing rate at closest approach) at t =
{degen_steps}; the particle cloud re-spread afterwards via maneuver-mode
diffusion, and the heavy-tailed likelihood prevents bias from these steps.

OUTPUT MARGINALIZATION
----------------------
state_estimates.csv reports the particle-weight marginal posterior over BOTH the
maneuver mode and the two bias states. cov_px..cov_vy are total
mode-marginalized Cartesian covariances computed from the full weighted
ensemble, i.e. E[P_mode] + between-mode spread (no spread is lost, so the
NEES-style proxy is not artificially small).

PROXY DIAGNOSTICS (GROUND TRUTH IS NOT PUBLIC)
----------------------------------------------
* pos_rmse / vel_rmse are PROXIES, not truth-based errors: time-mean posterior
